<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Talal ibn Rashid</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/1868">1868</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Talal ibn Rashid was emir of Jabal Shammar from 1848 to 1868, the son of the dynasty's founder <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abdullah-ibn-rashid">Abdullah ibn Rashid</a>. He consolidated the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emirate">emirate</a>'s hold over northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/najd">Najd</a>, encouraged merchants and pilgrims to pass through <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hail">Ha'il</a>, and undertook building works in the town. European travellers described him as an able and relatively tolerant ruler.</p></div>
